# Copilot Agent Mode Prompt — Discovery Agent: live + intelligent behavior (no layout change)

Do not restructure, reskin, reposition, or recolor any existing element. Additive only.

## Preserve exactly (zero diff)
Header (wordmark, Playbook Store, Search History, Log out, avatar), hero heading, source pills (IDP, Tachyon Agent Marketplace, Enterprise Git), mode tabs (Catalog Search, Intelligent Discovery), search input + button, Trending Now / Most Popular cards, "Or try" chips. Same DOM, classes, copy, style. No sidebar, no dark mode, no new palette/typography, no new nav.

## Add below the hero (currently empty space)

**1. Live status line** — under search bar: `<count> solutions indexed · updated <N>s ago` + pulsing dot. Count from stats endpoint. Ticks 1/sec, resets on refetch (poll 30–60s). Reserve height, no layout shift.

**2. Trending Now / Most Popular → functional toggle** — single-select, default Trending Now. On select: skeleton (~300–450ms) → card grid, sorted by growth or search volume. Card: type icon, id (mono), type label, 2-line desc, reuse count, growth %. Cap 6–8 cards, no pagination. Card click = no-op/TODO unless detail view exists elsewhere.

**3. Search** — debounce 250ms; Enter/Search button = immediate. Replaces grid with query results; empty query reverts to Trending/Most Popular. Chips fill input + trigger search. Zero-match = calm empty state, no red/error styling.

**4. Intelligent Discovery tab** — on search, render instead of grid:
- Summary: N related entries, strongest match id + reuse count
- "Reuse instead of build" callout with est. dev-days-saved range
- "Grounded in N matches" line
- Matched entities as §2 cards below

Zero matches: state plainly nothing matches, no fabricated results.
Switching back to Catalog Search preserves current query.

**API contract (typed client; mock now, real later):**
```ts
type Entity = { id:string; type:"component"|"agent"|"repo"|"prompt"; description:string; reuseCount:number; growth7d:number; searches7d:number };
GET  /api/catalog/stats                    -> { indexedCount:number }
GET  /api/catalog/search?q=&sort=trending|popular -> { items:Entity[] }
POST /api/catalog/ask  { query:string }    -> { summary:string; matches:Entity[]; estimatedSavingsDays:[number,number]; grounded:boolean }
```
Match existing repo API conventions if they differ — don't add a second convention.

**5. Corner notifications** — bottom-right, every 8–10s (first at ~2–3s). Kinds: new solution indexed, now trending, just reused, playbook published. Icon + label + id (mono) + auto-dismiss progress (~5–6s) + manual close. Max 2–3 stacked. `aria-live="polite"`, no focus-steal, no sound. Source from events endpoint if present; else local sample list isolated in one swappable function.

**6. Data honesty** — any mock count/%/reuse number gets a small "sample preview data" tag near the results header. Gate behind a `usingMockData` flag; auto-removes once wired to a real endpoint.

